{"action": "shared_understanding_confirmed", "at": "2026-08-28T13:13:37+00:00", "data": {"summary": "Implement a platform-neutral opening-balance preview and confirmation boundary over the verified kernel. Preview makes no stock change and returns exact SKU, pool/location, quantity, reason, resulting balance, version, and an opaque confirmation expiring in five minutes. expiresAt supports a future visible countdown; there is no minimum wait and no Block Kit GUI in this slice. Confirmation before expiry binds the exact action and authenticated-principal context to one caller-created commandId and evaluates it atomically. Exact retries using the same confirmation, commandId, and normalized contents recover the original terminal result even after expiry. Changed action, principal mismatch, reused confirmation under another commandId, or expiry before first confirmation fails closed and requires a fresh preview. Extend the existing repo-owned verifier for preview, expiry, restart persistence, binding, mismatch, replay, and no-mutation behavior. Defer GUI, service/auth transport, Cloudflare deployment, package publication, and production cutover. No commit, push, PR, merge, deployment, or publication is authorized."}, "event_id": "427f765c-3121-46cb-86fc-957c15ca7755"}
